Support modern HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and web applications to the extent supported by the underlying system WebView.

## 6.2 Browser Architecture

Do not render external websites by downloading HTML and inserting it into React.

Implement a proper browsing architecture using native Tauri/WebView capabilities.

Requirements:

- External websites should render inside browser webview instances.
- Browser content should be isolated from the privileged React application.
- Multiple tabs should have appropriately managed webview instances.
- Tabs should support navigation lifecycle events.
- Handle loading and navigation errors.
- Avoid unnecessarily loading inactive tabs.
- Manage webview resources when tabs are closed.
- Prevent arbitrary access to application filesystem permissions.

Tauri uses the operating system's webview rather than shipping a full Chromium browser.

Respect this architectural limitation.

Do not promise Chrome-equivalent browser functionality where the underlying engine cannot provide it.

